WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
On one Friday every spring,
many churches stand bare.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.640
Some hold a three-hour
service, from noon to 3.

3
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.010
Many Christians walk the
14 Stations of the Cross,

4
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.700
remembering Jesus' crucifixion.

5
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:18.330
It is a day of fasting,
remembering a death.

6
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.130
And yet its name is Good Friday.

7
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.290
So why do Christians call
the day Jesus died good?

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.110
In this mission, you'll
walk through Holy Week,

9
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.220
from palm crosses on Sunday
to bread and wine on Thursday.

10
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.760
Then you'll see Easter in
Britain today: chocolate eggs,

11
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.510
bank holidays, and fuller churches.

12
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: explain why Christians
call the day Jesus died good.
